                        "review": "TL;DR: It's fun, if you like driving games, this is *the* game to get\r\nThis is handsdown the best driving game I've played. If you're using a gamepad some of the controls can feel a little jarring to begin with, with a keyboard or a wheel it is much easier. At first it felt difficult to enjoy this game compared to ATS or ETS2 because of the realism and detail put into every aspect of this came, but overtime I've grown to appreciate it, so much so that I'd argue it's better than either of those games. The customizability in this game is amazing, with you being able to choose your vehichle, maps, controls, car physics, traffic, whether, time of day, and even including a mod manager for community mods inside the game. \r\nThis game is jam-packed with different kinds of activities for anyone that would be interested in a driving game. It has races, deliveries, bus driving, police running, challenges, a career mode, open world free roam, tutorials, etc. \r\nI've played this game for 50 hours and have not come across a single bug as of yet. And while my does not meet the recommended specs for this game, particularly the RAM, I have still been able to run this game relatively smoothly, with minor annoyances like longer loading times. \r\n\r\nLINUX: I'm not sure if this was a me problem, or a larger issue, the game would not register my wheel when running from Bazzite Linux. Using Nobara fixed this immedietly though - This is a driver issue and not the games fault\r\n(Works well on Windows and Linux)",
